Basic Analysis I by Jiri Lebl (@math-source-analysis: 0, is #reference) { r_00D018D5107F06EE77E9066592
Jiří Lebl, *Basic Analysis I: Introduction to Real Analysis, Volume I*, version 6.3, 15 May 2026. English. [Author's site](https://www.jirka.org/ra/), [official PDF](https://www.jirka.org/ra/realanal.pdf), [web edition](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/). The author describes an undergraduate analysis text requiring prior proof preparation; it also supports further study.

**Reading progression:** [1.2 real numbers](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_setofreals.html), [2.1 sequences](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_seqsandlims.html), [2.4 Cauchy sequences](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_cauchy.html), then sections 2.5–2.6 on series and [6.1 uniform convergence](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_puconv.html) / [6.2 interchange of limits](https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_liminter.html). Complete arguments and selected exercises, comparing their assumptions with the common lessons.

**Inspection, 1 November 2026:** PDF title/version/copyright; actual real-number completeness premise; sequence/monotone and Cauchy definitions and selected arguments; pointwise/uniform definitions and selected counterexamples; opening interchange discussion. Whole chapters, later derivative proofs and exercises are not claimed fully audited. The broader assignments remain learner work.

Copyright 2009–2026 Jiří Lebl. The author offers both CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and CC BY-SA 4.0; derivatives must retain at least one applicable licence and be marked. Keep source media external. These trail investigations are original; source figures and text are not bundled.
